  "lineage": "Japanese comic monologue storytelling performed by a lone seated rakugoka in formal kimono at a low cushion (zabuton) on the yose stage, using only a folding fan (sensu) and hand-towel (tenugui) as props. Developed from Edo-period temple-sermon anecdote into an urban entertainment codified in Edo (Tokyo) and Osaka lineages, its repertoire divides into classical koten and newly-written shinsaku pieces, each ending in the ochi (punch-line 'fall') that gives the form its name. The teller enacts a whole dialogue of characters by turning the head and shifting voice, all from the seated position; the delivery is naturalistic conversational speech shaped for comic timing.",
